# MaternalGuard MCP Server — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development. In production (Railway),
# set these as project-level Variables instead of shipping an .env file.

# ─── API key authentication (strongly recommended in production) ────────────
#
# When MCP_API_KEY is set, every POST /mcp request must include a matching
# X-API-Key header. When unset, the /mcp endpoint accepts any request
# (fine for local dev, NOT OK for a publicly-reachable deployment).
#
# Generate a strong secret with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
#
# Then configure Prompt Opinion's MCP server entry:
#   Authentication Type: API Key
#   Header Name:         X-API-Key
#   Header Value:        <the same secret you set below>
#
MCP_API_KEY=

# ─── Server port (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Defaults to 5000. Railway injects its own PORT at runtime and this value is
# ignored there. Override locally if 5000 is taken.
#
# PORT=5000

# ─── Panel scan (cohort triage tool) ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# When MATERNALGUARD_ENABLE_PANEL_SCAN=true, the MaternalPanelScan tool is
# registered with the MCP server. It scans the bundled patient list configured
# below, applies the deterministic urgency classifier, and returns a ranked
# triage queue with RED / YELLOW / GREEN urgency bands.
#
# This DOES NOT enumerate a live workspace. Live workspace enumeration is a
# future Prompt Opinion platform feature.
#
# MATERNALGUARD_ENABLE_PANEL_SCAN=true
#
# Comma-separated list of FHIR Patient IDs that make up the bundled cohort.
# Replace with the actual UUIDs that Prompt Opinion assigns after importing
# the FHIR bundles (Maria's bundle + the additional cohort bundle).
#
# MATERNALGUARD_BUNDLED_PATIENT_IDS=maria-santos-uuid,lin-zhang-uuid,amara-okonkwo-uuid,rachel-fisher-uuid

# ─── Governed FHIR write-back ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# When MATERNALGUARD_ENABLE_WRITEBACK=true, ProposeMaternalAction will persist
# draft Task and Flag resources to the FHIR store (with a Provenance audit
# record). Without it, ProposeMaternalAction returns a dry-run preview only.
#
# All persisted resources are in DRAFT status (Task.status=requested,
# Flag.status=inactive) and require a clinician to flip status to accepted /
# active before the action takes effect.
#
# MATERNALGUARD_ENABLE_WRITEBACK=true
